    "summary": ```A four-year-old boy named Ariel accidentally broke a rare 3,500-year-old bronze age jar while visiting the Hecht Museum in Haifa, Israel. The jar, which was one of the few complete artifacts from its period and used for holding wine or oil, was damaged when the child was momentarily unsupervised. Instead of being punished, the museum staff welcomed Ariel back warmly when he returned with his mother Anna Geller and presented them with a clay vase he had made.```,
